docs\architecture\system-architecture.md-737-| Event and statistic correctness                   | Cricket edge cases can silently produce plausible but wrong aggregates.                                                                                                                                                            | Preserve the approved identities/revisions, use corpus edge cases and independent golden results, property-test invariants, and make formula versions visible.                                                                         | Every event/statistic Pull Request.                                                                   |
docs\architecture\system-architecture.md-738-| Queue/cache consistency                           | A lost job or stale cache can publish statistics from superseded events.                                                                                                                                                           | Use atomic outbox/job creation, idempotent workers, data/definition-version cache keys, invalidation tests, and reconciliation jobs. Avoid these components until needed.                                                              | Before Intermediate rollout.                                                                          |
docs\architecture\system-architecture.md-739-| Live feed ordering, correction, licence, and cost | Late or duplicate events can cause divergence; provider terms may prevent redistribution.                                                                                                                                          | Select a licensed provider, persist provider sequence/idempotency keys, pass live data through normal validation, and test replay/reconciliation.                                                                                      | Optional Advanced gate.                                                                               |
